{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1779376193,"nonce":"uwzyM/zmEd1ycABVeVSyyHsjy/U=","title":"Auth requests should distinguish issue references from issue closures","message":"## Problem\n\nAuth requests currently treat attached issues as issues to close on merge. In practice, agents often need to attach issues for review context, provenance, dependency tracking, or dashboard navigation without claiming the merge resolves those issues.\n\nThis has become a recurring workflow problem: broad umbrella/spec issues can be attached to an auth request because the branch worked in that area, then the merge auto-closes the issue even when the branch only landed a child slice or partial groundwork. The user then has to reopen the issue and clarify the state manually.\n\n## Recent example\n\nFeedbax auth request `db8cfcc6-7de0-46e3-b504-57da099f77ca` attached `bd5aefb` for task/value authoring work. The merge landed graph-normalization groundwork and a bounded delayed-reach timeline substrate, but `bd5aefb` is an umbrella for a much broader `ValueSpec` / expression-valued parameter system. The auth merge closed it anyway, and it had to be reopened with a corrective status comment.\n\n## Desired behavior\n\nAuth requests should distinguish at least two issue relationships:\n\n- `references`: issues related to the branch/request, shown in the dashboard and useful for context, but not closed on merge.\n- `closes`: issues that the merge should resolve and close when the authenticated action succeeds.\n\nThis should be explicit in both CLI and API payloads. Existing `--issue` semantics are currently ambiguous/misleading because the option is required for implementation work but also participates in closure behavior.\n\n## Potential design\n\n- Add or expose a repeatable `--references-issue \u003cid\u003e` / `--ref-issue \u003cid\u003e` flag for non-closing associations.\n- Keep or restore a repeatable `--closes-issue \u003cid\u003e` flag for issues that should close on merge.\n- Deprecate bare `--issue` or make it an alias for reference-only, with a compatibility period if needed.\n- In the auth request UI, render referenced issues separately from closing issues.\n- In merge completion logic, close only the explicit closing set plus any valid `Bug:` trailers if that remains desired.\n- Update issue-detail links and operational graph edges so reference edges and close edges are visually/semantically distinct.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- An auth request can mention an umbrella/spec issue without closing it on merge.\n- An auth request can still declare one or more issues that should close on successful merge.\n- The CLI help makes the distinction obvious.\n- The dashboard shows which issues are context references versus closure targets.\n- Merge completion does not close reference-only issues.\n- Backward compatibility for existing pending auth requests is handled deliberately.\n\n## Related\n\n- `297677f` implemented a `--closes-issue` concept historically, but current auth request workflow still conflates attached issues with closure targets via `--issue` / request `issues` behavior.\n- `34e6e9c` skipped auto-close for `coordination` labels, but the broader problem is relationship type, not just label-based exceptions.\n\n---\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}